  "legacy_root_freeze": {
    "_comment": "STOP ACCRUAL (ADR-0562 §6 strangler). The legacy source roots are FROZEN SHRINK-ONLY. Every crate dir that lived under a `frozen_roots` entry at the freeze commit is listed in `crates` and is tolerated forever; a crate dir under a frozen root that is NOT listed is a crate BORN into a root the reorg exists to empty, and fails MEM-NEW-LEGACY-ROOT-CRATE. Removing a name is burn-down and is always allowed — it is also REQUIRED: a listed dir that is no longer a crate fires MEM-STALE-LEGACY-ROOT-BASELINE, so the census shrinks in lockstep with the moves and slack cannot outlive the debt it was granted for (the same contract crate-catalog-coverage's `uncatalogued` carries). PRODUCER-EMITTED, NEVER HAND-TYPED: `buck2 run //ci/facade/module-membership:oya-cloud-ci-capability-membership-app-bin -- --repo-root . --emit-legacy-freeze` prints this whole block from the gate's OWN collect(), so the census can never drift from the corpus the gate actually walks; the producer REFUSES to grow the census without --allow-new, so a regen cannot launder a newly-born legacy-root crate into the tolerated set. `frozen_roots` is deliberately NOT spelled `roots`/`scan_roots`: it is not coverage-bearing (an emptied frozen root does not go vacuous, it goes maximally strict — every crate born there is new), so it is correctly outside cloud-ci-scan-root-liveness scope and carries no anti-narrowing debt when a drained root is finally retired. Burned 24 cloud/** rows same-change with the founder dev push c2ee2631a \"Delete cloud directory\" (clean slate; kuberos/k8s regenerate via port engine).",
